<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">CERN</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as European Organization for Nuclear Research</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">CERN, the European Organization for Nuclear Research, is an intergovernmental particle physics laboratory founded in 1954 on the Franco-Swiss border near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>. It operates the world's largest particle accelerators, including the Large Hadron Collider, with which the Higgs boson was discovered in 2012. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-wide-web">World Wide Web</a> was invented there by Tim Berners-Lee in 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cern.jpg" alt="CERN" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Organization for Nuclear Research Organisation européenne pour la recherche nucléaire · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CERN_logo_badge.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Universal Postal Union was established at Bern in 1874, the League of Nations met in Geneva from 1920, and after 1945 the city hosted the European office of the United Nations, the World Health Organization and many other bodies, while <b>CERN</b> was founded beside it in 1954.</blockquote><a href="/empire/swiss-confederation">Swiss Confederation · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Coinage is credited to the Kingdom of Lydia and the World Wide Web to <b>CERN</b>, where Tim Berners-Lee invented it in 1989; nuclear fission, discovered in Berlin, and the jet engine, made by Hans von Ohain and Frank Whittle in Germany and England, are credited to no state…</blockquote><a href="/essays/who-invented-it-first">Who Invented It First?</a></li><li><blockquote>The web, created at <b>CERN</b>, spread rapidly and transformed communication.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-6">6 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>At <b>CERN</b> in Geneva, Berners-Lee circulated 'Information Management: A Proposal' for a hypertext system linking documents across computers.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-12">12 March in history</a></li></ul></section>
